# Privacy Policy

Last updated: November 2, 2026

VisBal ("us", "we", or "our") operates the Duck Coin Planner mobile application (the "Service").

We are committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how our application handles data, permissions, and third-party services.

## 1. Local Data Storage & User Privacy
We value your privacy and design our app to be as secure as possible. **We do not collect, store, or transmit your personal financial or trip data to our own servers.** 

There are no user accounts required to use the Service. The following information is stored exclusively on your device:
* Income and spending entries
* Trip logs and related details
* Notes
* Receipt photos
* Application configuration and settings

Because this data is stored entirely on your device, we have no access to it.

## 2. Device Permissions (Camera and Photos)
To provide key features, the application requires access to your device's Camera and Photo Gallery:
* **Usage:** These permissions are used solely to let you capture new receipt photos or pick existing photos from your device.
* **On-Device Processing:** The application uses Google ML Kit to scan and read text from your receipts. This text recognition happens entirely on your phone. 
* **Storage:** Scanned receipt images are saved directly to your phone’s local gallery. No photos or extracted text are ever transmitted to us.

## 3. Advertising and Third-Party Services
The application displays advertisements provided by Google AdMob to remain free to use. While we do not collect your information, Google AdMob may automatically collect certain data to serve and measure advertisements, including:
* Your device's unique Advertising ID
* Device manufacturer, model, and operating system details
* IP address (primarily used to determine general location for localized ads)

### Regulatory Consent (EEA and UK)
For users residing in the European Economic Area (EEA) and the United Kingdom (UK), the app displays a consent prompt in compliance with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR). You can choose whether to allow personalized ads, non-personalized ads, or revoke consent at any time through the app settings.

You can review how Google handles this data by reading the [Google Privacy & Terms Policy](https://google.com).

## 4. Internet Use
The application utilizes your device's internet connection for two specific purposes:
* To load and display advertisements via Google AdMob.
* To download required font files the very first time you generate a PDF report. 

No user data or financial entries are uploaded during these connections.

## 5. Backups and Exports
The application allows you to back up or export your data (such as financial summaries or trip reports). 
* **User Control:** Data exports and backups are created strictly when you explicitly choose to generate them.
* **Destination:** Exported files are saved locally on your device or shared through native device menus to locations of your explicit choosing (e.g., your personal cloud storage, email, or messaging apps). We do not host or have access to these backups.

## 6. Data Deletion
You retain complete control over your data. You can delete individual income/spending entries or trip logs directly inside the app interface at any time. 

To permanently delete all data, notes, receipt text, and settings associated with the app, simply uninstall the application from your device. 

## 7. Children's Privacy
Our Service is not directed at or designed for children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect or request personally identifiable information from children. Because all user input is stored locally on the device and never sent to our servers, no children's data is ever collected, tracked, or retained by us.

